note: head pitch: the nose sits — (not read: no part tagged nose) of the way from the eye midpoint to the mouth (frontal 0.474..0.630); the stem, eye midpoint -> mouth, is 0.569 of the bar (frontal 0.510..0.675); frontal ranges read on demo, scarf, the rig-c/trailer character; the turn is not reported (src/propose.ts FRONTAL_REFERENCE says why)
note: breath: chest translatey 4.44 px peak to peak (amp 2.22, base 2.22) = 2.5 % of the torso's length, 177.2 px (neck [424, 258] -> hip [403, 434]), once per 40-frame idle at 12 fps
note: hair_front (head:front hair): bang_r, bang_c, bang_l are a template, not its locks — columns at 0.25, 0.5 and 0.75 of the face box's width, along the head's down axis (the eye line's perpendicular, roll 4.844 degrees), each rooted on the part's art; the opaque shape does not separate the locks painted inside one mass of hair, so a lock that runs elsewhere is not followed — move the chains onto the locks
note: handwear is two blobs: one sleeve chain per mesh, and nothing on chest
note: topwear ends at y=436 (hip 434): no robe chains -- add a sash chain by hand if one hangs
note: bottomwear (full:bottomwear): its art starts 71.1 px below chest's origin, so it hangs from the waist — its mesh takes the hip line and its skirt chains, no chest segment, and the breath does not carry its root
note: legwear (full:legwear): no rule -> region on hip
note: mesh spacing: grid 29 = round(H / 37), H 1087 rig px the height of every part's box together (rows 49 to 1136), in place of a tenth of each part's short side (hair_back 17 -> 29, hair_front 16 -> 29, hairpin 9 -> 29, neck 6 -> 29, handwear_r 26 -> 29, handwear_l 25 -> 29, topwear 18 -> 29, bottomwear 22 -> 29; kept, already as coarse: none); r is the part's own. Calibrated on three figures of similar size (H 1106-1185 rig px, issue #265 Stage A), where every check bar passed at this divisor and the idle moved by up to 1.427 rig px against the finer lattice — no bar reads that. propose --grid-rule part drafts the part's own spacing
LINT hairback_r and hairback_l on mesh 'hair_back' squeeze it: swung together, every other bone held, edge 27-26 of triangle 135 closes to 0.407 times its rest length at idle frame 22 (max(ratio, 1/ratio) 2.455; <= 1.926544 is required, check's TEXTURE_STRETCH bar) — vertex 27 rides hairback_r2 0.73841, vertex 26 rides hairback_l2 0.89913; alone, hairback_r reads 1.420 and hairback_l 1.424. Their tips are 55.0 px apart and their amplitudes are opposed (hairback_r [0.6, 1.4, 2.4], hairback_l [-0.6, -1.4, -2.4]), so their tips swing towards each other and apart: give both the same sign (then 1.051), or drop one chain
